.TH PATINA-SESSION-CTL 1 "2026-10-19" "patina-desktop 0.1.0" "Patina Desktop"
.SH NAME
patina-session-ctl \- log off, restart, shut down or lock the Patina session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patina-session-ctl
.BR logout | reboot | poweroff | lock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patina-session-ctl
asks the running Patina session to end or lock.
.B logout
ends the session, and the login screen comes back.
.B reboot
and
.B poweroff
show "Restarting…" or "Shutting down…" and ask systemd-logind; if it refuses (for example,
another user is signed in and authorisation is needed), the desktop comes back.
.B lock
locks the screen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
and
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
name the session, as inside it they always do.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patina-session (1),
.BR patina-lock (1)
